  data.frame(id = 1L, files = I(list(ids)))
)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

With \code{convert = "auto"}, \code{Attachments} columns are read back as list-columns
of attachment IDs, which you can pass to \code{grist_attachment_download()}.

Attachments that are no longer referenced by any cell may still appear in
\code{grist_attachments()} for a while.
